# Footnotes

A reference is a label in brackets after a caret[^1], and its definition can
be written anywhere in the document[^where]. Notes are numbered in the order
they are first referred to, so a label is only a name[^1].

[^1]: The first note. Hover over a number to read its note in place.

[^where]: Under the paragraph that cites it, or at the end.

    A longer note continues on lines indented by four spaces, and may hold:

    - a list
    - or any other block

Every note is collected in a section at the end. `footnote` is replaced by
`Footnote.svelte`, which shows the note beside its number. A bracket that is
not a footnote is escaped, \[^like this], or put in code, `[^abc]`.
